# Frontend Architecture

## Principle

Users should **only see** nav, dashboards, records, and actions they are authorized for. Hide unauthorized UI; backend still enforces.

## Shell model

```
Application Shell → Auth (role + permission + scope) → Sidebar + Header + Content → Allowed features
```

Context required: who am I, company, role, department, team, permissions, scope.

## Route groups (conceptual)

- `(platform)` → `/platform|super-admin/*` — Super Admin
- `(organization)` / `(company)` → `/[companySlug]/*` — company management
- `(workspace)` → employee AI Workspace (`chat`, `conversations`, `usage`, `roi`)
- `(auth)`, `(onboarding)` — unauthenticated / setup flows

Routes are not security. Middleware + API scopes must match RBAC.

## Navigation

Config-driven items: `{ label, path, permission, scope }`. Filter by role + permission + scope. Do not scatter `if (role === 'CEO')` everywhere.

## Dashboards = same engine, different scope

| Role | Aggregation scope |
|------|-------------------|
| CEO | Company |
| Dept Manager | Department |
| Team Lead | Team |
| Employee | Self |

Drill-down: Company → Department → Team → Employee → AI Request → Conversation. Breadcrumbs reflect **viewer scope only**.

## Features by concern

Colocate under `src/features/<domain>/` (`api/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `schemas/`). Shared UI in `src/components/`. Config in `src/config/`. RBAC in `src/lib/rbac/`.
